  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_6841892137514b92833f6010aeb0a2e9",
      "statement": "celld is an alpha that is not safe for hostile multi-tenant use, and security fixes apply to the latest release only.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security.md#L3-L5",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e248196e81add361c00f42cb877f6fd1190a1f008bd528a6e8bf0ef76f0e2388:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c57b9a7556b44fdf896e5bbcf2e09471",
      "statement": "One fleet runs one application and celld trusts the application code, fleet nodes, and operators; it depends on two external boundaries — a trusted private network for the internal listener and object storage credentials restricted to one fleet bucket.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security.md#L8-L18",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:22d57c916c6d249245e2a56c0c56abfb2cfa75f213d1ac542fa0df1a333914ba:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bf6b09b7cdfe441dbd370607883eb92d",
      "statement": "The public listener serves the deployed Worker and reserves only /.well-known/celld/health, while the internal listener serves the peer protocol and operator API, defaults to an ephemeral loopback port, and returns 404 for an unknown path rather than passing it to the Worker.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security.md#L21-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:64a705b6105962b15f3a010ead1d1f4fc1b6d931a0b466f0286bc632920209ac:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7dc4efe53a7b4a0ba7242aa85267dd20",
      "statement": "An explicit advertised address requires an explicit internal-listener address and celld rejects an explicit non-loopback public listener without one; celld cannot verify a hostname or translated port, so the operator must route the advertised address to the internal listener.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security.md#L32-L38",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dc455c4e0e4f55efb47583d134d468c09369cc238b25c46e9aca84c069dd3ae1:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7ae77b7dcfab414fb808adcf1dbb13bf",
      "statement": "The internal listener has three request groups: unauthenticated operator routes, the /peer/tunnel establishment that carries the fleet HMAC with a clock limit and replay protection, and the peer-control and reserved-cell routes that use the fleet HMAC; all three require the trusted private network.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security.md#L55-L68",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:691505e18e05a1446b8d91f749ebd483d3d10b64914117d05f77340791194625:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_98c341660e524ee495c2aa2abd9e2a09",
      "statement": "The peer authentication protocol version is 5 and the signature domain is cells-peer-request-v1.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/peer_auth.rs#L16-L22",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:31c13c9ac9fe43d545a3d79571e74c929af83a7899897be4cdde69abd836c814:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0a439a0ceeff4b71a88b1ab010470575",
      "statement": "The peer signature is HMAC-SHA256 over a canonical request of domain, protocol version, method, path and query, body hash, source, target, timestamp, and nonce.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/peer_auth.rs#L251-L269",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b7f93aa115b2883d3006766f2e9305c52cbe52f96e2d5c37b4181a1cc57d30df:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c39ef15ed97f4af285cc6bbd95355719",
      "statement": "The signed headers are x-cells-peer-version, x-cells-peer-source, x-cells-peer-target, x-cells-peer-timestamp, x-cells-peer-nonce, x-cells-peer-body-sha256, and x-cells-peer-signature.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/peer_auth.rs#L159-L175",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:df0b56ceb6012665324407c4ff8ee417b2b565e972d9288cebb47195098f3f00:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cfd0ae1faf3f4caeb2da8cdc1979d1c4",
      "statement": "Verification checks the protocol version, validates the source and target identities, enforces a 30-second clock window, compares the body hash, verifies the signature, and then checks the target against the expected node session.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/peer_auth.rs#L178-L228",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:81d8bbbc9c5650058619829e5af32f11521c4844255c87eda49b1798a3cf8119:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_09069d6583eb409a820d9361d743d688",
      "statement": "Replay protection keeps a bounded nonce cache with a 60-second retention; a repeated nonce is rejected and a full cache returns ReplayCapacity.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/peer_auth.rs#L230-L244",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7b8d9f0e4ec5ec50ca95044947bb7c77229adbec295c5fb64e2b839a41f8a7ee:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_79ff69caf02343b89f7e70679d55957b",
      "statement": "The peer tunnel is an h1 upgrade on /peer/tunnel after which the connection is an opaque duplex stream carrying literal HTTP; per-call control rides x-cells-* headers that node A overwrites and node B strips, and idle tunnels are pooled per peer for sequential reuse.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/main/peer_tunnel.rs#L3-L20",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:73a7ad40ac276335793ae316e57f208c0d92719c3e157349d11c0a99d253a057:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6bb923da186041b7bcabd5bf5173e551",
      "statement": "The tunnel permits a request body to stream to the owner, so the fleet HMAC cannot sign an individual call; the establishment signature decides who can open a tunnel, it does not authenticate bytes after establishment and does not encrypt traffic, so the private network remains the boundary.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security.md#L70-L76",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:279ecefb31c67752e2a478f61cb25671d9f046dff315d818f6e873a53340d3ae:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cdb40af361ba441d95e5c8537e1cf31b",
      "statement": "celld does not terminate TLS on either listener; terminate public TLS at an ingress proxy and use an encrypted overlay for the internal listener when the network does not provide confidentiality.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security.md#L78-L80",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:313dc5f41c68058ef5dfd3f4f1ab336fc82ed329893c9c8b641c8b383c83cf2f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ccd461ebba644463926eaf29c6b7487d",
      "statement": "The node lease refuses to publish without a signed-probe key.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/ownership_store.rs#L428-L432",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c7900ba4fd9c4923e27c916bbc32a5a3145a310c8125ccf01d25602b49ab76a0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_066888fe77f44463a668be9462afd4dc",
      "statement": "A signed peer probe uses the separate cells-peer-probe-v1 domain, carries a challenge, and the response is verified for identity and challenge match before acceptance.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/peer_probe.rs#L110-L179",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2bd89308ca4510d176cb2b27975aa87af4b95caf111555582e5079ca9fa992f4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_394f5e62b86d42ffb434fc5ccf66f8d3",
      "statement": "celld ignores X-Forwarded-Host and X-Forwarded-Proto by default and trusts them only when a trusted proxy replaces both; it always takes the path and query from the request target, and the Host header controls request.url but is not made trustworthy for authorization.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security.md#L105-L124",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:273eef26928edaa5fc2a833d89b5d7dca268cd1d18d881598ae597485c526117:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2d1561331d5e419eb0cef7c1df476023",
      "statement": "The public listener and /do/<ID> have a 1 GiB default request body limit (CELLD_MAX_REQUEST_BODY_BYTES), return 413 for an oversized declared body or a read past the limit, and stream a /do body when its declared length is at least 1 MiB or unknown.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security.md#L126-L135",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ecb070d98423e69f8f9154c4b712e70c4ade512c2daea20b52e509050cadb05d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1d85ad8a82054f1a8c2d8b4804a8a552",
      "statement": "The fleet bucket is the root of authority, so a person holding its credentials controls the fleet; each credential should access one fleet bucket only and be replaced after a suspected disclosure.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security.md#L137-L145",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:507aa212e5c54360273ed7b9fced8ad266d2dba6dcbe8c7500209c32b45abf4f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_edf38d8f37784d219929c14d88fa5502",
      "statement": "A managed deployment nudges the node to adopt the deployment pointer, with an escape hatch CELLD_CLOUD_RESTART_ON_DEPLOY (off by default) that re-executes the process image instead of adopting in place.",
